\section*{Integral \#9 (Medium)}
\[
\mathcal{L}_t\left\{\cos(\omega t-\phi)\right\}(s)=\int_0^\infty e^{-st}\cos(\omega t-\phi)\,dt
\]
Solution Methodology:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Apply angle sum formula: $\cos(\omega t-\phi)=\cos(\omega t)\cos(\phi)+\sin(\omega t)\sin(\phi)$
    \item Break up the integral into two integrals: 
    \[
    \mathcal{L}_t\left\{\cos(\omega t-\phi)\right\}(s)\cos\phi=\mathcal{L}_t\left\{\cos(\omega t)\right\}(s)\cos\phi+\mathcal{L}_t\left\{\sin(\omega t)\right\}(s)\sin\phi
    \]
    \item \textbf{Know your Laplace Transforms!} Or....
    \item Preform IBP$\times2$ on each integral and recover the implicit recurrence relations
    \item Solve for the individual integrals
    \item Combine and simplify
\end{itemize}
\[
\boxed{\;\mathcal{L}_t\left\{\cos(\omega t-\phi)\right\}(s)=\frac{s\cos\phi+\omega\sin\phi}{s^2+\omega^2}\;}
\]

